<title>RUSSIA: Russia, Kazakhs discuss Orenburg gas joint venture.</title>
<headline>Russia, Kazakhs discuss Orenburg gas joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian and Kazakh presidents, Boris Yeltsin and Nursultan Nazarbayev, discussed the joint development of gas reserves around the Russian border city of Orenburg on Saturday.</p>
<p>&quot;It was about the joint exploitation of the very substantial reserves of gas in the Orenburg region, joint exploitation, joint financing, joint transport and the offer of products on the external market,&quot; said Kremlin spokesman Sergei Yastrzhembsky after the two leaders met for 20 minutes near Moscow.</p>
<p>He gave no other details.</p>
<p>--Moscow newsroom +7 095 941 8520</p>
</text>
